      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** Metformin tops out at 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets. Many clinicians stay at or below 2,000 mg/day. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is about twice the maximum. It raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nI suspect a typo or a unit mix-up. Possible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided into doses\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is what you meant. If you confirm it, I'll enter it with a note that the dose was verified, but I'd advise against it. If this is for a new start, you may also want to titrate up gradually, for example starting at 500 mg once or twice daily."
      }
     ],
